Given a string, print all the letters present at the odd index, followed by the letters present at the even index.
Input
afdg5tg
Output
fgtad5g
=====
s=input()
oddchar=s[1::2]
evenchar=s[::2]
finalstr=oddchar+evenchar
print(finalstr)


or


s=input()
s1=""
s2=""
for i in range(len(s)):
    if i%2!=0:
        s1+=s[i]
    elif i%2==0:
        s2+=s[i]
print("%s%s"%(s1,s2))
